    "answer": "Here is a financial comparison of Amazon, Apple, Alphabet, Microsoft, and NVIDIA based on their latest full fiscal years. \n\n**Revenue:**\nAmazon led with $716.92B (FY2025, ended 2025-12-31), followed by Apple with $478.83B (FY2026, ended 2026-09-26), Alphabet with $402.84B (FY2025, ended 2025-12-31), Microsoft with $331.84B (FY2026, ended 2026-06-30), and NVIDIA with $215.94B (FY2026, ended 2026-01-25).\n\n**Operating Income:**\nApple posted the highest operating income at $158.06B (FY2026), closely followed by Microsoft at $155.24B (FY2026). NVIDIA reported $130.39B (FY2026), Alphabet reached $129.04B (FY2025), and Amazon recorded $79.97B (FY2025).\n\n**Net Income:**\nMicrosoft led in net income with $133.75B (FY2026). Apple followed with $132.18B (FY2026), Alphabet with $132.17B (FY2025), and NVIDIA with $120.07B (FY2026). Amazon reported the lowest net income at $77.67B (FY2025).\n\n*Note: Fiscal years end on different dates and do not cover the exact same calendar period.*",
